# Cursor AI Rules & Mandatory Pre-Coding Checklist

- ALWAYS use Bun as the package manager (`bun dev`, `bun run build`, `bun run typecheck`, `bun run check`, `bun test`, `bun run format`). Never use npm/yarn.
- MANDATORY LOGIC SEPARATION: Keep JSX presentational components clean of inline business logic, API calls, or side-effects. Extract state to custom hooks in `src/feature/<feature-name>/hooks/` and backend logic to `services/`.
- MANDATORY SERVICE TESTING: Add `<service-name>.test.ts` for any service file created in `services/`.
- Place domain feature code in `src/feature/<feature-name>/`.
- Keep Next.js App Router files in `src/app/` as thin wrappers that render `src/feature/<feature-name>/index.tsx`.
- Place atomic UI primitives in `src/components/ui/` using `cva`, `cn()`, and `@radix-ui/react-slot` (`asChild`).
- Use Tailwind CSS v4 semantic tokens (`bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `bg-primary`, `border-border`). Do NOT hardcode colors.
- After code edits, verify with `bun run verify`.
